ot/pull/123140.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #117207\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n`update_node_from_node_modification()` is the heavy-lifting function responsible for re-applying modifications made in an inherited scene, when it's affected by file reimport. There can be edge cases where it fails to fully apply modifications, for example when setting one property of a node opens up possibility of setting other properties on it. The reason is it's only ever using the initial property list from the freshly instantiated node as a filter (after set_script).\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n- converts the original process to multi-pass, so that it can pick up updates to the property list.\r\n- *depends on* #123133 because to correctly apply the modifications, one must first obtain those modifications, which requires properly implementing `_property_can/get_revert`.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123140/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123140/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}